 ('ENT_RAS_RASTAFARI','PER_RASTAFARI','Hub collective for the Rastafari movement, a living Abrahamic-derived Jamaican (Caribbean / worldwide) religion founded in the 1930s; publicly attested in scholarship (Barrett; Edmonds).'),
 ('ENT_RAS_JAH','PER_RASTAFARI','The supreme God of Rastafari; the name derives from Jehovah/YHWH and is publicly central to Rastafari practice and reasoning (''I-and-I''). Attested throughout Barrett and Edmonds.'),
 ('ENT_RAS_HAILE_SELASSIE','PER_RASTAFARI','Emperor of Ethiopia (1930-1974); venerated by many Rastafari adherents as the returned Christ or as divine. Modeled neutrally as a belief held within the tradition. Publicly attested (Barrett; Edmonds).'),
 ('ENT_RAS_MARCUS_GARVEY','PER_RASTAFARI','Jamaican Pan-Africanist leader (1887-1940) received within Rastafari as a prophet-forerunner who foretold the crowning of an African king. Publicly attested historical figure (Barrett; Edmonds).'),
 ('ENT_RAS_BABYLON','PER_RASTAFARI','Rastafari theological concept for the corrupt, oppressive system of Western/colonial society and its institutions, drawn from the biblical Babylon. Publicly attested (Barrett; Edmonds).'),
